Just a note before e-mailing off to the buglist folks.

While playing the newest version (3.0j) that I ftp'd yesterday, I 
read a scroll of destroy armor (HACKUM MUCH or somesuch). It 
destroyed my shield. When it asked me what to call it, it said the
name of the scroll was garbage (%$!@#) and asked me what to 
call it. I called it destroy armor and inventoried again to see what
else I could get rid of (trying to pick up armor on level 3). I saw the
same scroll in the same inventory slot! When I read it again, it 
did exactly the same thing (destroying my helmet this time). I
inventoried again and it was still there. Then I read the book I had
at the time. When I went down to level 4, it crashed (sorry, don't 
remember the exact error). And then it locked up tight on the "G" in
Goodbye on the screen before the score list.

I had to cold boot.

I have a 386 PC running PC-DOS 3.3 with CtrlAlt as the only TSR 
and the windows (himem.sys, 386emm.sys, smartdrv.sys) drivers
and nnansi.sys drivers loaded. I have 539k available before running
the game (I was running the version from last week and if I had
Norton Guides, a 72k TSR, loaded, it crashed the game, so I've been
checking before entering the game). 

I deleted all save/bone/level files before installing and backed up
my .cnf file.

